  <Properties>
    <pitchId>
      <Value><![CDATA[spotify-for-silence]]></Value>
    </pitchId>
    <title>
      <Value><![CDATA[Spotify for Silence]]></Value>
    </title>
    <tagline>
      <Value><![CDATA[40 million tracks. Not a single sound.]]></Value>
    </tagline>
    <demoFeatures>
      <Value><![CDATA[Shuffle Silence
Quiet Wrapped
Mute Premium
Shh Radio]]></Value>
    </demoFeatures>
    <cardsEpic>
      <Value><![CDATA[License all the world's silence | Negotiate rights to every quiet moment. Libraries want 70%. Summer houses are holding out.
End the open-plan office | Not physically. Just acoustically. One headset at a time.
Lossless silence, 24-bit | Hi-fi nothing for audiophiles who can hear the difference. They can't. They pay.
Silence Wrapped | The yearly recap: 'You heard nothing for 41,000 minutes. Top genre: Awkward.'
Own the pause | Every pause in every meeting, powered by us. 'This silence was sponsored by.'
Silence for Teams | Enterprise plan: a whole department quiet at once. HR calls it a culture initiative.]]></Value>
    </cardsEpic>
    <cardsStory>
      <Value><![CDATA[Mute the sales team | As a developer, I want a playlist that covers Sales so that I never learn what 'circle back' costs.
Skip this silence | As a user, I want to skip to the next silence so that I get one that is a little less quiet.
Any questions? | As a project manager, I want to play the 'any questions?' silence so that the meeting ends itself.
Collaborative playlist | As a couple, I want a shared playlist so that we can not talk about it together.
Suspicious silence alert | As a parent, I want an alert for the silence that means marker pens so that the sofa survives.
Shuffle | As a user, I want shuffle so that I am surprised by which nothing comes next.
Offline mode | As a commuter, I want my silence downloaded so that I can hear nothing even in a tunnel.
Lyrics view | As a karaoke fan, I want lyrics for every track so that I can not sing along correctly.
Silent standup | As a scrum master, I want a 15-minute silent track so that the daily is finally timeboxed.
Royalties for mimes | As a mime, I want to be paid per stream so that my life's work is finally heard.
Julefrokost lull detection | As a host, I want an alert when the julefrokost goes quiet so that I can deploy more gløgg.
Save that silence | As a tech lead, I want the silence after 'who deployed on Friday?' saved so that we can cherish it.]]></Value>
    </cardsStory>
    <cardsFeature>
      <Value><![CDATA[Discover Weekly: new pauses | Thirty fresh silences every Monday. You have not heard any of them before. Probably.
Sleep timer | Stops the silence after 30 minutes so that it finally gets quiet.
Premium: ad-free silence | The free tier is interrupted every 15 minutes by a man shouting about offers.
Volume slider | Goes to 11. Nothing happens. Users report feeling more in control.
Genre: Small Town Sunday | Field-recorded. One distant lawnmower at 2:14, then nothing.
Crossfade | Blends one silence seamlessly into the next. Twelve developers, three sprints.
Awkward lift radio | A curated station of lifts, waiting rooms and 'so... anyway'.
Workout mix | The same silence, but at 140 beats per minute.
Live sessions | A real person being quiet in real time. Tickets from DKK 249.
Podcast: Two Guys Say Nothing | Two hosts, one hour, no opinions. Number one in every category.
Remastered 2026 edition | The classic silences, now 12% quieter.
Mute button | Mutes the silence. The PO insisted. We don't know what it does either.
Friend activity | See that your colleague is listening to nothing. Just like in the daily.
Car mode | Back seat edition: the nine seconds between two 'are we there yet?'.
Christmas silence playlist | The moment after somebody asks who is doing the washing-up.
Radio based on this silence | More silences like this one. The algorithm is copy and paste.]]></Value>
    </cardsFeature>
    <cardsBug>
      <Value><![CDATA[Track contains a cough | Silence #4412 has a cough at 0:37. User demands a refund and an apology.
Silence is buffering | Stream stalled and the user heard nothing instead of nothing. Three angry tickets.
Wrong silence on shuffle | Expected: Forest Lake at Dawn. Actual: Dinner with the In-Laws. User is shaken.
Search returns no results | Technically correct for every query. QA and the PO disagree on whether it is a bug.
Volume 0 louder than volume 3 | Inverted somewhere. Nobody can hear the difference, so nobody can verify the fix.
Ad played during 'Deep Calm' | Meditating user got 'ARE YOU READY FOR BLACK FRIDAY?'. User is no longer calm.
Silence plays at 1.5x speed | A podcast setting leaked. Users say the silence feels rushed. Cannot measure.
Autoplay started a podcast | When the silence ended, two men began discussing crypto. Severity: highest.]]></Value>
    </cardsBug>
    <cardsTechdebt>
      <Value><![CDATA[All 40 million tracks are one file | silence_final.mp3, symlinked 40 million times. The storage bill is suspiciously fine.
Recommendations are Math.random() | Nobody has complained in four years. Do not tell data science.
The file is not actually silent | There is a faint fridge hum from the founder's kitchen. It is now 'the brand sound'.
Track length stored as text | 'About three minutes.' Sorting a playlist by length gives vibes, not order.
No tests, because tests are noisy | CI is muted 'for consistency'. The build has been red since March. Quietly.
Licences tracked in Silence_v3_NEW(2) | The sheet says who owns which silence. Its owner left in 2022. Silently.]]></Value>
    </cardsTechdebt>
    <cardsCeo>
      <Value><![CDATA[Otto Request: Can it play music too? | 'Just as a little extra.' That is the competitor. That is the entire competitor.
Otto Request: Silence, but with AI | 'Generative. Personalised.' The model outputs nothing. The demo went great.
Otto Request: Make it louder | Feedback from the board: they could not hear the product during the demo.]]></Value>
    </cardsCeo>
    <siteHeroHeadline>
      <Value><![CDATA[40 million tracks. Not a single sound.]]></Value>
    </siteHeroHeadline>
    <siteHeroSub>
      <Value><![CDATA[Streaming for people in open-plan offices. Curated silences for focus, sleep and the moment right after someone asks 'any questions?'.]]></Value>
    </siteHeroSub>
    <siteCta>
      <Value><![CDATA[Play nothing now]]></Value>
    </siteCta>
    <sitePillars>
      <Value><![CDATA[Lossless nothing | 24-bit, 192 kHz silence. Our audiophile users swear they can hear the difference. We nod.
Curated by experts | Our editors are a librarian, a lighthouse keeper and a tester who hasn't spoken since the reorg.
Works offline | Download your silence and hear nothing anywhere: tunnels, planes, family birthdays.]]></Value>
    </sitePillars>
    <siteTestimonials>
      <Value><![CDATA[(Silence.) ... (More silence.) Five stars.
I played 'Awkward Pause Vol. 2' in a sprint review. The client approved everything.
The free version has ads every 15 minutes. So it's just my open-plan office again.
My Wrapped said 41,000 minutes of nothing. My mother is finally proud.]]></Value>
    </siteTestimonials>
    <sitePricingJoke>
      <Value><![CDATA[Free with ads (a man shouting 'SALE'). Premium: DKK 59 a month for nothing. Literally.]]></Value>
    </sitePricingJoke>
    <siteFooterLine>
      <Value><![CDATA[© Spotify for Silence. All silences are licensed. Please do not hum along.]]></Value>
    </siteFooterLine>
